    "body": "## Description\n\n`get_geometry3k_sft_dataset` stores `processed_input[\"image_grid_thw\"].squeeze(0)`, which turns the processor's `[num_images, 3]` grid into a flat `[3]` vector. Every consumer expects one row per image: `FSDPEngine` and the Megatron `extract_vision_from_multi_modal` `torch.cat` the per-sample grids along dim 0, and the Qwen-VL vision tower indexes `grid_thw[:, i]`. With the squeezed grid, Geometry3K SFT on a Qwen-VL model fails in the vision forward (and a batch of several samples would be concatenated into one flat vector). The CLEVR SFT loader and `VisionRLVRWorkflow` already store the grid unchanged.\n\nReproduction with a tiny randomly initialized `Qwen2VisionTransformerPretrainedModel` (no download):\n- `grid_thw=[[1, 2, 2]]` (as the CLEVR loader stores it): OK, output `(4, 16)`\n- `grid_thw=[1, 2, 2]` (as the Geometry3K loader stores it): `TypeError: iteration over a 0-d tensor`\n\nThis stores the grid as the processor returns it.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNone found (searched open and closed issues and PRs).\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`). I ran `ruff check` / `ruff format` on the changed files only.\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable; built with `./docs/build_all.sh`)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [ ] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n**Breaking Change Details (if applicable):**\n\nN/A\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThe new test `test_vlm_sft_image_grid_thw_keeps_one_row_per_image` in `tests/test_vlm_sft_dataset.py` covers both the Geometry3K and CLEVR SFT loaders with a fake Qwen-VL processor that returns `image_grid_thw`; on `main` the Geometry3K case fails (`[1, 2, 2] != [[1, 2, 2]]`) and the CLEVR case passes. With the fix, all 10 tests in the file pass (CPU only; GPU tests not run).\n\nAI use: I used an AI coding assistant (Claude Code) while writing the fix and tests; I reviewed the changes and ran the checks listed above.\n",
